        "severity": "WARNING",
        "location": "engine/runtime/opencode_json.go:86",
        "claim": "The trailing-content check only refuses when decoder.Token() succeeds. For trailing non-JSON text after the object (e.g. `{...} garbage`), Token returns a syntax error, so the check passes and the file is treated as valid. Install then rewrites the file and silently drops the trailing text. The claim that a file that is not one JSON object is left as it is does not hold for this input. A backup is written, but no refusal is reported.",
        "evidence_class": "inferential",
        "causal_disposition": "introduced",
        "proof_refs": [
          "engine/runtime/opencode_json.go:86-88"
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "F2",
        "severity": "SUGGESTION",
        "location": "engine/runtime/opencode_json.go:182-188",
        "claim": "When an owned entry is removed and mcp.servers is left empty, removeOpenCodeJSON deletes the servers container (and mcp if empty) even if the owner's file already held an empty `servers: {}`. Deleting that container is outside the owned entries. Separately, uninstall rewrites and reformats the file without keepOnce, so a file that uninstall changes gets no backup.",
        "evidence_class": "inferential",
        "causal_disposition": "introduced",
        "proof_refs": [
          "engine/runtime/opencode_json.go:182-188",
          "engine/runtime/opencode_json.go:271-274"
        ]
      }
